.TH boar 1  "boar 0.7.27" 
.SH NAME
boar \- Build On Available RAM: RAM\-aware Cargo wrapper
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBboar\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICARGO ARGS\fR...]
.PP
\fBboar\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fBcargo\fR \fICARGO\-COMMAND\fR [\fICARGO ARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
BOAR — Build On Available RAM
.PP
boar is a RAM\-aware Cargo wrapper for Linux. It places a project's
Cargo target directory on tmpfs when the machine has enough safe
headroom, and falls back to disk when it does not. Memory pressure
(PSI) and live swap activity are checked before each automatic
placement; when pressure is elevated, builds run on disk even in
\fBauto\fR mode.
.PP
boar requires Linux. Each project's RAM target lives under the RAM root
(default /dev/shm/boar) and is marked with a .boar-owner file so that
\fBboar clean\fR only removes boar\-managed directories.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBboar build\fR, \fBcheck\fR, \fBtest\fR, \fBrun\fR, \fBbench\fR, \fBclippy\fR, \fBdoc\fR
Run the corresponding Cargo subcommand through BOAR, with the target
directory placed on RAM or disk per the active mode.
Example: \fBboar build \-\-release\fR
.TP
\fBboar cargo\fR \fICARGO\-COMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
Run any Cargo subcommand through BOAR.
Example: \fBboar cargo metadata \-\-no\-deps\fR
.TP
\fBboar status\fR
Show memory capacity, pressure (PSI), RAM root usage, and active
RAM\-backed targets with their owners and sizes.
.TP
\fBboar clean\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR]
Without \-\-all, remove the current project's RAM target. With \-\-all,
remove every BOAR\-owned RAM target.
.TP
\fBboar doctor\fR
Check Linux, Cargo, memory, pressure, and tmpfs readiness, and report
any condition that would force disk builds.
.TP
\fBboar init\fR
Create a documented .boar.toml in the current workspace. Fails if the
file already exists.
.TP
\fBboar help\fR
Show the built\-in help message and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fIauto|ram|disk\fR
Placement mode. Default: \fIauto\fR. Env: \fBBOAR_MODE\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-reserve\-mib\fR \fIMIB\fR
Minimum RAM to leave for the OS. Default: adaptive (25% of RAM, 2 GiB
floor). Env: \fBBOAR_RESERVE_MIB\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-ram\-mib\fR \fIMIB\fR
Cap the RAM BOAR may use for the target. Default: unlimited.
Env: \fBBOAR_MAX_RAM_MIB\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-ram\-root\fR \fIPATH\fR
Directory for RAM\-backed targets. Default: /dev/shm/boar.
Env: \fBBOAR_RAM_ROOT\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-disk\-target\fR \fIPATH\fR
Disk fallback target directory. Default: the workspace's \fItarget\fR/.
Env: \fBBOAR_DISK_TARGET\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-monitor\fR, \fB\-\-no\-monitor\fR
Enable or disable the live pressure monitor (default: enabled).
Env: \fBBOAR_MONITOR\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Settings are resolved with the precedence: CLI options, then environment
variables, then .boar.toml, then built\-in defaults. Run \fBboar init\fR
to create a documented configuration file. A typical .boar.toml:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mode = "auto"
# reserve_mib = 2048
# max_ram_mib = 8192
ram_root = "/dev/shm/boar"
disk_target = "target"
monitor = true
.fi
.RE
.PP
Unknown keys in .boar.toml are rejected.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .boar.toml
Per\-project BOAR settings in the workspace root.
.TP
.I /dev/shm/boar/
Default RAM root. Each project target is a subdirectory tagged with a
\&.boar\-owner marker file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/boar/estimates/
Persisted per\-project target\-size estimates used for placement
decisions (fallback: ~/.cache/boar/estimates/).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBBOAR_MODE\fR, \fBBOAR_RESERVE_MIB\fR, \fBBOAR_MAX_RAM_MIB\fR, \fBBOAR_RAM_ROOT\fR, \fBBOAR_DISK_TARGET\fR, \fBBOAR_MONITOR\fR
Override the corresponding settings (see OPTIONS).
.TP
\fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
Locate the estimate cache.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success. For cargo subcommands, the exit status of the cargo process.
.TP
2
Usage or runtime error (unknown option or command, invalid mode,
missing cargo, non\-Linux platform).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
boar build \-\-release
Build on RAM (or disk under pressure) with release profile.
.TP
boar \-\-mode=disk test \-\-workspace
Force disk placement and run the workspace tests.
.TP
boar status
Inspect memory headroom and RAM targets.
.TP
boar clean \-\-all
Reclaim every BOAR\-owned RAM target.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR baby (1),
.BR birthd (1),
.BR cargo (1)
.SH VERSION
v0.7.27
